{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"How to Preview and Test","role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" calls into a real ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance"},{"text":". For previews and tests, swap it for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — an actor that records every call and exposes its history for assertions. The mock has no Mixpanel dependency and runs offline."}]},{"anchor":"In-a-SwiftUI-preview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"In a SwiftUI preview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inject a mock-backed store and the analytics work flows without spinning up the SDK:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["#Preview {","    let store = AppStore.configured(analyticsService: MockMixpanelAnalyticsService())","    return ContentView().environment(store)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This requires that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppStore.configured"},{"type":"text","text":" accepts an injected "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":". See Swidux’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/Swidux\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" guide for the factory pattern."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"In a Swift Testing suite","anchor":"In-a-Swift-Testing-suite","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the mock to verify mapper behavior. Await the plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":" to make assertions deterministic:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","import Testing","","@Test","func incrementMapsToCounterAdded() async {","    let mock = MockMixpanelAnalyticsService()","    let store = AppStore.configured(analyticsService: mock)","","    store.send(.counter(.increment(5)))","    await store.analyticsPlugin.flush()","","    let events = await mock.trackedEvents","    #expect(events.first?.name == \"counter_added\")","    #expect(events.first?.properties[\"amount\"] == .int(5))","}"]},{"level":2,"text":"Asserting on identify and alias","anchor":"Asserting-on-identify-and-alias","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The mock records identify and alias calls in order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@Test","func userSignInIdentifies() async {","    let mock = MockMixpanelAnalyticsService()","    let store = AppStore.configured(analyticsService: mock)","","    store.send(.auth(.signIn(userID: \"user-1\")))","    await store.analyticsPlugin.flush()","","    let calls = await mock.identifyCalls","    #expect(calls == [.init(userID: \"user-1\", properties: [\"tier\": .string(\"free\")])])","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an actor, so its accessors are async — wrap them in ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/howtopreviewandtest"]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" from SwiftUI previews and Swift Testing suites without touching Mixpanel’s network."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVe